# FRAGMENT — do not replace the whole demo.conarium.dev site with this.
# Existing handles (/t/*, /proof, /healthz) stay. Insert ONLY the
# @wellknown handle immediately ABOVE the catch-all redir.
# First matching `handle` wins.
#
# Why: MCP clients (Claude) probe RFC 9728 / RFC 8414 paths when adding
# a connector. They expect 404 on a public unauthenticated demo. The
# catch-all 302+HTML is parsed as OAuth metadata, Dynamic Client
# Registration runs, and the connector dies with
# "Couldn't register with ...'s sign-in service".
# Do NOT serve fake OAuth metadata. 404 is the honest answer.
#
# Apply (patron / Claude — Hetzner write):
#   1. Edit the live Caddyfile (usually /etc/caddy/Caddyfile)
#   2. caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   3. systemctl reload caddy
# This repo copy does not reload Caddy.

	@wellknown path /.well-known /.well-known/*
	handle @wellknown {
		header Content-Type "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
		respond "not found" 404
	}

	# existing catch-all — keep below the matcher above
	# handle {
	# 	redir https://conarium.dev/#trylive
	# }
